# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: autocad-symbol-case-preserved -- AutoCAD keeps the case its own code interned a symbol with (vlax-vbEmpty, variant, safearray)
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

Found reconciling type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad and
vlax-vb-constants-unbound (AutoCAD 2022 suite run 20261023T074943Z):
(vl-symbol-name 'vlax-vbempty) is "vlax-vbEmpty" on AutoCAD -- the case
AutoCAD's own code interned the symbol with, not the upper case the
reader would give. VARIANT / SAFEARRAY ("variant" / "safearray") are the
same mechanism; clautolisp 2.3.42 implements only those two (a print-name
override; identity and reading unchanged). BricsCAD upper-cases all of
them.

* To do

Probe the print name of every symbol AutoCAD predefines (atoms-family 0
on a fresh drawing, vl-symbol-name of each) to find which are not upper
case, then generalise AUTOLISP-SYMBOL-PRINT-NAME to a measured table
(AutoCAD dialects only), as for VARIANT / SAFEARRAY.

* Batched probe prepared 2026-10-29 (branch prep-pending-probes)

probes/sources/probe-pending-divergences.lsp (suite "pending-divergences",
group symbol-case) captures this on real hardware. Run it via
probe:suite:{autocad,bricscad}:windows / :macos when the Windows runner is next
online (one session covers all three data-blocked issues). clautolisp baseline
validated 2026-10-29.
